    "id" : "S2344",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Enumeration Type Names with \"Flags\" or \"Enum\" Suffixes",
    "description" : "This rule ensures enumeration type names do not redundantly include the suffixes \"Flags\" or \"Enum\".",
    "explanation" : "## Why is this an issue?\n\nThe information that an enumeration type is actually an enumeration or a set of flags should not be duplicated in its name.\n\n### Noncompliant code example\n\n    enum FooFlags // Noncompliant\n    {\n        Foo = 1\n        Bar = 2\n        Baz = 4\n    }\n\n### Compliant solution\n\n    enum Foo\n    {\n        Foo = 1\n        Bar = 2\n        Baz = 4\n    }",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
